{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolumeSaddle","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolumeSaddle","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume","lean:module:QOU.Knot.Clausen","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.LocalExtr.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Order.LocalExtr","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Order.Compact"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.neg_two_Cl_2_at_five_sixths","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.neg_two_Cl_2_at_five_sixths","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSaddle.lean#L272-L278","doc":"**E3 corollary — the saddle max is attained at `x = 5/6`.**\n`−2Cl₂(2π·(5/6)) = 2Cl₂(π/3)` — the Kashaev saddle location. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.neg_two_Cl_2_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.neg_two_Cl_2_le","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSaddle.lean#L262-L270","doc":"**E3 corollary — the saddle max bound.** For `x ∈ [0,1]`,\n`−2Cl₂(2πx) ≤ 2Cl₂(π/3)`: the continuum saddle functional is bounded by the\nfigure-eight volume `Vol(4₁) = 2Cl₂(π/3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.neg_Cl_2_pi_div_three_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.neg_Cl_2_pi_div_three_le","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSaddle.lean#L209-L260","doc":"**Saddle brick E3c — the global minimum of `Cl₂` (sorry-free).** On\n`[0, 2π]`, `Cl₂(θ) ≥ −Cl₂(π/3)`. Compactness gives a minimiser; it is\ninterior (the endpoints give `0`, but `Cl₂(5π/3) = −Cl₂(π/3) < 0` by E2+E3b);\ninterior minimisers are critical (`IsLocalMin.deriv_eq_zero` +\n`hasDerivAt_cl_2`), so by E3a the minimiser is `π/3` or `5π/3`; positivity\n(E3b) rules out `π/3`. Hence the minimum is `Cl₂(5π/3) = −Cl₂(π/3)`.\n(bean qou-yzs2) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_kashaev_le_log_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_kashaev_le_log_add","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSaddle.lean#L184-L207","doc":"**Saddle brick E1, upper half (sorry-free).** `log kashaev` exceeds the max\nlog-term by at most `log N`: the sum of `N` terms is at most `N · max`.\nTogether with the lower half, `(2π/N)·log kashaev` and `(2π/N)·max log-term`\ndiffer by at most `(2π/N)·log N → 0` — the `log(Σ) ≈ max log-term` step of\nthe saddle asymptotic at exponential scale (bean qou-3g69). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_sup_le_log_kashaev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_sup_le_log_kashaev","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSaddle.lean#L169-L182","doc":"**Saddle brick E1, lower half (sorry-free).** The max log-term bounds\n`log kashaev` below: a single nonneg term is at most the sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.one_le_sup_kashaevProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.one_le_sup_kashaevProd","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSaddle.lean#L160-L167","doc":"The largest Kashaev term is at least `1` (witnessed by the `k = 0` empty\nproduct) — the positivity the log-squeeze needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_kashaevProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_kashaevProd","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSaddle.lean#L123-L158","doc":"**Saddle brick E5a (sorry-free).** The log of the Kashaev term is twice the\nlog-sine Riemann sum: `log(kashaevProd N k) = 2·Σ_{j=1}^{k} log(2 sin(jπ/N))`\nfor `k < N` — the bridge from the Kashaev product to the E4 sums.\n(bean qou-sho7) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.saddle_critical_point_two_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.saddle_critical_point_two_pi","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSaddle.lean#L91-L121","doc":"**Saddle brick E3a (sorry-free).** On the full interval `(0, 2π)` the\ncritical-point equation has exactly TWO roots:\n`2 sin(θ/2) = 1 ↔ θ = π/3 ∨ θ = 5π/3`. Extends `saddle_critical_point`\n(which covers `(0, π)`) by reflecting through `sin(π − x) = sin x` on the\nupper half. `θ = 5π/3` is where `Cl₂` attains its minimum `−Cl₂(π/3)` —\nthe Kashaev saddle the volume emerges from (bean qou-yzs2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.saddle_critical_point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.saddle_critical_point","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSaddle.lean#L65-L89","doc":"**The saddle critical point (dual-purpose).** On `(0, π)`,\n`2 sin(θ/2) = 1 ↔ θ = π/3`. This is the location of the Kashaev\nsaddle — the factors `4 sin²(πj/N)` of `kashaevProd_eq_sin` cross `1` here —\nand it is *simultaneously* the critical point of the QOU dilog-saddle\npotential `V(θ) = Im Li₂(e^{iθ})`, whose derivative is `−log(2 sin(θ/2))`\n(content block `rem:dilog-saddle-regime`): `V'(θ) = 0 ⟺ 2 sin(θ/2) = 1 ⟺\nθ = π/3`, giving `Vol(4₁) = 2 Cl₂(π/3)`. The block states this narratively;\nthis is its Lean proof, needing no Clausen function — only `sin(π/6) = 1/2`\nand injectivity of `sin` on `[−π/2, π/2]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_eq_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_eq_sin","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSaddle.lean#L50-L63","doc":"**The Kashaev product in sin form.** The `k`-th factor of the figure-eight\nKashaev invariant is `4ᵏ (∏ⱼ₌₁ᵏ sin(πj/N))²` — the `2 − 2cos = 4sin²`\nrewrite that turns `log ⟨4₁⟩` into a Lobachevsky Riemann sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.two_sub_two_cos_two_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.two_sub_two_cos_two_mul","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSaddle.lean#L43-L48","doc":"The factor identity `2 − 2cos(2x) = 4 sin²x` (from `cos 2x = 1 − 2sin²x`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}